`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------'

 V1.0: - Non Cli version, it worked, but it was an non AGA version, so Mr Guru
         visited many times. Hd went unvalidated :(
         This version was not released...


 V2.0: - First Released version

       - Works well

       - No bugs found yet


 V2.1: - Found a bug myself... Problem with the buffering... Bug fixed!

       - Some text longer than 80 characters, and was not looking nice in a 
         message. Bug Fixed!

       - When the allfiles.cfg uses the folowing line: SECTIONS 1-123 
         and some sections were not available, the program stopped...
         Bug found by Cor de Bruin from AGA Ehq... Bug fixed!    
         

 V2.2: - A complete rewritten version...
       
       - Added the logfile option in the Newfiles.cfg..
         if you put 'on' on the the third line in this config, TNF will create
         a Newfiles.log in your Tron:log/ directory.. This is for locating
         problems (if there are still any)

       - Added System Requesters... If an error may ocure, you'll get a 
         system request, telling you what's wrong..

  
V2.2B: - Oops, at the beginning of a new month TNF created a NewFiles list 
         that was realy F***ed... Bug Fixed...


 V3.0: - Rewritten the whole source in an other programming language
     
       - Added Filesize to the list

       - Program is much smaller

       - Program is not faster, but it works better than the V2.x versions,
         because of the date searches...


 V3.1: - More Speed! Paul told me that he had an offset longword in the Filecat
         , so the program is now 400% faster :)

 V3.2: - If you have FileAreas with a number higher than 999 (and there is
         someone who has that!), The area's wouldn't be checked! FIXED IT!

       - If you have more than 2 Allfiles/Newfiles lists, the last lists
         are the same... Shame on me!! FIXED IT!

       - When i moved or killed a file from my FileCat, TNF din't skip it,
         so you have that file in you're list, but in the wrong area, or
         the file doesn't exsits at all!  FIXED IT!!
 
       - Thanx to Pascal Dreissen, Streamline BBS!
